# ── Generated art ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This block REVERSES an earlier decision recorded here, and the reversal is
# the point, so the old reasoning is kept rather than deleted:
#
#   "art/blockout/ and art/renders/ ARE tracked on purpose: hero_models.py is
#    not byte-reproducible, so the generated art cannot be rebuilt exactly and
#    has to be versioned rather than regenerated."
#
# That is true about reproducibility and wrong about what to do. Because the
# build is not byte-reproducible, every rebuild rewrote ~200 MB of binaries
# with different bytes for identical geometry, and git keeps every version
# forever. Tracking them made the repository grow by the full art payload on
# each build. It was also tracked TWICE: art/blockout (107 MB) and its synced
# copy in game/assets (104 MB), out of ~230 MB total.
#
# The real fix is to make the build runnable by anyone (done: no hardcoded
# paths) and publish art as release artefacts.
#
# art/reference/ is deliberately NOT here: those are downloaded 3-view drawings
# and their authored region sidecars. They are INPUTS, nothing regenerates
# them, and no verification result is reproducible without them.
art/blockout/
art/textures/
art/renders/
art/silhouettes/
art/verify/
game/assets/units/
game/assets/icons/
art/icons/

.dem_cache/

# Per-unit child scripts written by tools/build_all.py, removed after each run.
tools/.build_*.py
